From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Owner Placeholder <owner@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:17:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc/asm: use the Clang DS-form constraint whenever Clang
 parses the headers

DS_FORM_CONSTRAINT picks "Z<>" for Clang builds and "YZ<>" otherwise,
keyed on CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG. With CONFIG_RUST=y in a GCC build, bindgen
parses the same headers with libclang: CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG is unset, the
inline asm in asm/atomic.h (arch_atomic64_read/set) and asm/uaccess.h
gets "YZ<>", and libclang rejects the unknown "Y" constraint, which
fails the bindings for every 64-bit configuration built with GCC.

Key the choice on __clang__ instead, which is defined both for Clang
builds and whenever libclang parses the headers. Code generation is
unchanged: GCC still sees "YZ<>", and bindgen never emits code for inline
asm.

Signed-off-by: OWNER NAME <owner@example.invalid>
---
 arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h
index f48e64490..3080b4c9d 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h
+++ b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h
@@ -37,7 +37,12 @@
 #define STDX_BE	stringify_in_c(stdbrx)
 #endif
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG
+/*
+ * Clang has no "Y" constraint. Besides Clang builds, this also covers
+ * bindgen, which parses the headers of a GCC build with libclang and
+ * rejects "YZ<>" in the inline asm of atomic.h and uaccess.h.
+ */
+#ifdef __clang__
 #define DS_FORM_CONSTRAINT "Z<>"
 #else
 #define DS_FORM_CONSTRAINT "YZ<>"
